{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779908-thallain-redcap-kith-the-powries","id":779908,"title":"Thallain Redcap Kith - The Powries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-04T10:08:25-08:00","id":779908,"title":"Thallain Redcap Kith - The Powries","content":"This is a kith that I created to use in my own games. Now that we have a proper Changeling: the Dreaming forum, I thought that I'd share it here in case anyone else was interested in using it for their own.<br /> <br /> <b>Powries</b><br /> <br /> Powries see themselves as ghastly death given form, and few survivors of an encounter with one would disagree. These Thallain cousins of the redcaps have an insatiable thirst for murder that can never be quenched. A powrie lives for the moment when he can next soak his wool cap in the blood of his victims.<br /> <br /> Powries despise their redcap relatives with a passion, even if they must often hide among them. The powries regard the redcaps as pretenders who have stolen the fear and reputation that rightly belongs to the powries. They claim that they are the true redcaps, and that their Kithain cousins, whom they call dunters, began to imitate their hunting habits to gain more respect.<br /> <br /> Most changelings remain blissfully unaware of the existence of the powries, and the few redcaps that learn of it will cover it up. They do this mainly out of fear that their own kith will suffer if the other changelings started hunting the powries. These redcaps see the rivalry between themselves and the powries as a personal conflict. Outsiders are not welcomed by either side.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Powries dress to intimidate. Most favor leather or gang colors, but some choose to wear a mask when hunting to capitalize on the fear of slashers instilled in the public by popular culture. In their fae mien, powries are almost indistinguishable from their redcap cousins, with grayish skin and stocky builds. The notable difference between a powrie and a redcap is that the powrie\u2019s teeth are sharp and pointed rather than blunt. To fae sight, the powrie\u2019s wool cap seems to drip with fresh blood. The Mists conceal this blood from mortal sight.<br /> <br /> <b>Lifestyles:</b> Powries are murderous by nature, and they usually choose to live in places where violence is common and frequently unreported. A powrie seeking to lay low for a time may seek employment in a slaughterhouse, but most powries will choose a life of crime, or simply collect what they require from their victims. Some powries will instead choose a nomadic lifestyle, terrorizing an area briefly and moving on before the authorities can react.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Childlings</b> inevitably display signs of future serial killers, frequently torturing and killing small animals or engaging in petty vandalism. It is not uncommon for a powrie to murder his mortal parents before setting out into the world on his own.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Wilders</b> are the powries that are most likely to band together. In the modern day, these gangs are invariably nomadic, due to their murderous needs. Wilders that remain solitary will generally seek to blend in with the local Unseelie redcaps, sometimes even joining a corby to keep up appearances. If a powrie can swallow his disdain of his Kithain cousins long enough to pull off the deception, he will inevitably become the cruelest and most brutal member of the band. <br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Grumps</b> tend to haunt desolate locations close to popular travel routes. In ancient times, this was easier for them, but the slums of modern cities have proven to be fertile hunting grounds for the powries. Some grumps will seek to make a name for themselves in the Unseelie Court or the Shadow Court, but most are content to be horrific urban legends to other changelings.<br /> <br /> <b>Affinity:</b> Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights</b><br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Relentless Ambush:</b> A powrie\u2019s chosen quarry is never safe. When a powrie is hunting a victim that is actively fleeing from him, he may move instantly to ambush his retreating prey. To do this, the powrie must step into a place of concealment, then spend a point of Glamour to move instantly to another place of concealment close to their prey. The powrie\u2019s victim must be within his line of sight, but unable to see the powrie when he activates this Birthright.<br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Ravenous Maw:</b> Like their redcap cousins, powries are gifted with a vicious bite that easily shreds flesh and splinters bone. A powrie\u2019s bite has a base damage of Strength + 3 (difficulty 5), and he is able to spend Glamour in an attempt to sever a limb using the same system as Kithain redcaps. The powries lack the unique digestive system of the redcaps, however. While powries are able to devour flesh and bone, they are strict carnivores, so even fruits and vegetables can leave them with indigestion. More exotic fare cannot be consumed, but a powrie is still capable of damaging such things with his bite.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailties</b><br /> <br /> <b>\u00b7 Butcher\u2019s Grim Cap:</b> According to some mortal legends, if a redcap does not frequently dye his cap in the blood of his victims, the cap will dry out and the redcap will die. For the powries, this is a sad reality. When a powrie\u2019s cap dries out, the powrie will begin to suffer a point of aggravated damage for each day that he goes without dyeing his cap in the blood of his victims. This damage takes the form of a painful withering, and it cannot be healed in any way until the powrie dyes his cap with the blood of a fresh victim. A powrie\u2019s cap will remain soaked for a number of weeks equal to the powrie\u2019s permanent Glamour rating if the victim he has slain is a human or changeling. A powrie is also able to utilize the blood of an animal he has killed to soak his cap, but it will only remain soaked for number of days equal to the powrie\u2019s permanent Glamour rating. To dye the cap properly, the amount of blood must be sufficient to fully soak the cap, so a powrie relying on small animals for their blood may require many victims. If a powrie\u2019s cap is ever destroyed, the powrie immediately gains a permanent dot of Banality and must immediately seek out a new wool cap as a replacement.<br /> <br /> <b>Quote:</b> <i>Pleasant evening, isn\u2019t it? What brings you to this lonely place?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T21:23:10-08:00","id":783917,"title":"","content":"When I've thought about a Thallain variant for redcaps the first place my mind has gone was always to give them the chicken claws. Regular redcaps can have this as a flaw (KB: Redcaps) meaning outsiders can still easily be misled, but these would have it as a birthright. They'd still suffer penalties on Dex rolls involving fine motor control, but the claws would act as agg damage sources (similar to fuath from Denizens). They'd also give bonuses to climbing rolls, being able to puncture any material short of iron, making it all the harder for any quarry to ever truly escape them.<br /> <br /> Still, your version's not bad! Love the Frailty. It's exactly what I would hope for. And making them more about killing than hunger is on the money. I'd go further and remove Ravenous Maw entirely, with just a note that they can consume the raw flesh of anything they killed with no ill effect in Relentless Ambush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T17:41:58-08:00","id":784434,"title":"","content":"I like this a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T18:27:47-08:00","id":785671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flimflamberge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779908-thallain-redcap-kith-the-powries?p=783917#post783917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I've thought about a Thallain variant for redcaps the first place my mind has gone was always to give them the chicken claws. Regular redcaps can have this as a flaw (KB: Redcaps) meaning outsiders can still easily be misled, but these would have it as a birthright. They'd still suffer penalties on Dex rolls involving fine motor control, but the claws would act as agg damage sources (similar to fuath from Denizens). They'd also give bonuses to climbing rolls, being able to puncture any material short of iron, making it all the harder for any quarry to ever truly escape them.<br /> <br /> Still, your version's not bad! Love the Frailty. It's exactly what I would hope for. And making them more about killing than hunger is on the money. I'd go further and remove Ravenous Maw entirely, with just a note that they can consume the raw flesh of anything they killed with no ill effect in Relentless Ambush.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad that you liked it. Your idea of the chicken claws is a pretty good one, though I'll probably stick with Ravenous Maw for my games. Ultimately, I gave them the Ravenous Maw birthright to maintain the fear of being eaten and to allow them to blend in with their redcap cousins, as a redcap that never bites through weird crap would quickly seem suspicious to other redcaps. As an added bonus, it also helps to explain the odd artwork of redcaps with pointy teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:40:14-08:00","id":786451,"title":"","content":"That's a very good point with the teeth. I typically wrote that off as artists working with insufficient information or redcaps who'd deliberately filed their teeth to points, but the latter doesn't always fit and the former is dull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}